  "description": "Kalapuya – The Ultimate E-Tandem for Off-Road Adventure and Performance\nNamed after the stunning Kalapuya mountain range in western Oregon, the Kalapuya Tandem is built for riders who demand peak performance in the most challenging environments. Whether you're tackling steep forested mountainsides, twisting gravel descents, or navigating rocky outcrops, the Kalapuya Tandem delivers outstanding stability, power, and control on both unpaved and paved terrain. Its advanced design and cutting-edge features make the Kalapuya perfect for those seeking adventure and high-performance versatility.\nWith Co-Motion’s zonally-butted ACMUltra7 aluminum tubing and a Co-Motion 1.5” TA carbon fork, this tandem offers the perfect combination of lightness, strength, and precision handling. Equipped with your choice of Shimano or SRAM eTap drivetrain options, disc brakes, and Gates Carbon Drive timing belt, the Kalapuya gives you the power and control to conquer any trail, while its performance options allow it to transition seamlessly between off-road and road riding.\nKey Features:\n\nOptimized for 700c wheels with 35-45mm tires for smooth handling on both gravel and pavement\n\nLight and tough Co-Motion zonally-butted ACMUltra7 aluminum tubing for a strong, lightweight frame\n\nTapered head tube & Co-Motion 1.5” TA carbon fork for superior precision and stability\n\nDisc brakes & hydraulic-ready cable routing for responsive braking in any condition\n\nBoost 148x12mm and 110x15mm TA dropouts for enhanced wheel stability and durability\n\nRack & fender mounts for touring flexibility and added convenience\n\nGates Carbon Drive timing belt for a smooth, low-maintenance ride\n\nCNC-machined chainstay yoke for added strength and performance\n\nInternal Di2 wiring ports & Hydro brake mounts for a clean, modern setup\n\nChoose the optional Rolf Prima carbon wheelset and fast road tires, and you'll be able to easily switch between off-road adventures and paved road speed. Whether you're tackling epic gravel climbs or cruising on smooth pavement, the Kalapuya Tandem has you covered for both.\nOur Shimano mechanical or Di2 and SRAM AXS drivetrain options offer an incredibly reliable shifting experience, ensuring every ride is smooth and powerful.",
